  "releaseNotes": "Consolidate and simplify several areas:\n      - RequestModel: Replace repetitive MakeXXXRequest method bodies with expression-bodied delegations to MakeCustomRequest, reducing duplication and centralizing request construction logic.\n      - ClientTransport: Add an IPEndPoint constructor, preserve the original DNS hostname for SSL/TLS validation, and resolve DnsEndPoint to prefer IPv4 when available (fall back to first resolved address). Minor connect-state handling adjustments to avoid redundant comments and keep the connect flow consistent.\n      - SslClient: Replace the old async BeginAuthenticateAsClient + callback flow with a synchronous AuthenticateAsClient using SslClientAuthenticationOptions (sets TargetHost, protocols, application protocol and disables revocation check). Remove/comment out the old ProcessHandshake callback, set handshake flags and trigger receive/handshaked events immediately. Add basic exception logging and ensure DisconnectAsync on failure.\n      - Buffer: Only return arrays to the pool when marked pooled, set the pooled flag after allocation, optimize Append for empty input and direct UTF-8 writes into the buffer, and add random-access APIs: WriteAt overloads (byte/span/char/generic), and ShiftAt/UnshiftAt to create/remove gaps at offsets. These changes add flexible in-place writes and safer pool management.\n      Overall: reduces duplication, improves DNS/address handling, simplifies SSL handshake logic, and extends buffer capabilities for arbitrary writes and shifts.k",
